Normal flow: PSU Event Hub → core_tst.mqs_athn_mtr.ehubstream → Bronze → Silverish → Raw Enrichment

Recovery flow: Backup/cleaned data core.radar_live.ehubstream_cleaned → same downstream Bronze → Silverish → Raw Enrichment

So when he asks “Do we have a proper testing plan yet?”, your data-focused test plan can be:

First checkpoint – identify and reconcile both data sets
Get the count/unique message IDs coming from PSU.
Get the count/unique message IDs from the cleaned backup data.
Confirm both populations can be identified separately in TST.
Validate the recovered data
Check that the header fields that caused the original failure are now correctly populated.
Compare a sample against the cleaned source.
Reconcile through each layer
Cleaned/PSU source → Bronze → Silverish → Raw Enrichment.
Identify any missing or unexpectedly rejected records.
Duplicate/overlap check
This is particularly important now because TST contains PSU + backup data.
Check whether the same business/message ID exists from both sources and whether this causes duplication downstream.
Downstream impact
Confirm recovered records are processed exactly like normal records and the downstream transformations/filtering haven't been affected.
